{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557676-rituals-of-haven-protection-and-clairvoyance-and-similar-powers","id":1557676,"title":"Rituals of Haven Protection and Clairvoyance and similar powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-16T07:20:26-08:00","id":1557676,"title":"Rituals of Haven Protection and Clairvoyance and similar powers","content":"Hello everyone! I was having this argument with a friend of mine regarding the limits of Rituals or protection, be they enacted by Blood Sorcerers lik the Tremere or Mages. So, the point in discussion is wheter it should be no problem for a being like an elder to use Astral Projection or Clairvoyance powers in havens proteced by said rituals, the question here is if the protection against the intrusion would be able to also cover such powers. I'd love to hear some thoughts regarding the topic as I myself am still not sure about which approach is more fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T12:24:29-08:00","id":1557680,"title":"","content":"My rule of thumb is that a method of magic scrying requires a counter for the specific method. However, I allow some counters to work in cases that are implicit rather than explicit in RAW.<br /> <br /> For example, Astral Projection uses an umbral body, so something like Ward vs Spirits would work. Rituals or powers that trigger on 'intrusion' or 'presence' (like Visceratika, Hearth Path, Krainas) should also react to umbral intrusions. A Gargoyle may sense the presence of an umbral entity in a room, but may not be able to pinpoint it.<br /> <br /> Completely remote powers (Scrying, Clairvoyance) are countered with powers or Rituals that affect the mind. More often than not a player complaint is that Clairvoyance is overpowered because it can not be detected - but it can, that's what the Awareness ability is for. I would also allow Auspex 1 to highten that sixth sense.<br /> Of course, a Neonate can not counter an Elder's Auspex 6 with their Obfuscate or Chimerstry, but something like Hearth Path 3 or Dementation 2 may be surprisingly effective. I'm partial to letting a creative solution work, even if it is with a lower power.<br /> <br /> I think some kinks in the protection of a Haven <i>should </i>be difficult to cover, at the very least for the benefit of players of Clans or splats that are able to exploit them - if I make warding Havens against Wraith spies too easy, I take that option away from the Giovanni player.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T15:13:22-08:00","id":1557687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557676-rituals-of-haven-protection-and-clairvoyance-and-similar-powers?p=1557680#post1557680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My rule of thumb is that a method of magic scrying requires a counter for the specific method. However, I allow some counters to work in cases that are implicit rather than explicit in RAW.<br /> <br /> For example, Astral Projection uses an umbral body, so something like Ward vs Spirits would work. Rituals or powers that trigger on 'intrusion' or 'presence' (like Visceratika, Hearth Path, Krainas) should also react to umbral intrusions. A Gargoyle may sense the presence of an umbral entity in a room, but may not be able to pinpoint it.<br /> <br /> Completely remote powers (Scrying, Clairvoyance) are countered with powers or Rituals that affect the mind. More often than not a player complaint is that Clairvoyance is overpowered because it can not be detected - but it can, that's what the Awareness ability is for. I would also allow Auspex 1 to highten that sixth sense.<br /> Of course, a Neonate can not counter an Elder's Auspex 6 with their Obfuscate or Chimerstry, but something like Hearth Path 3 or Dementation 2 may be surprisingly effective. I'm partial to letting a creative solution work, even if it is with a lower power.<br /> <br /> I think some kinks in the protection of a Haven <i>should </i>be difficult to cover, at the very least for the benefit of players of Clans or splats that are able to exploit them - if I make warding Havens against Wraith spies too easy, I take that option away from the Giovanni player.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's someething I agree with tbh. Astral Projection being countered by such methods makes sense. Clairvoyance CAN be extremely OP depending on how many powers the ST allows one to combine it with imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T20:00:45-08:00","id":1557694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557676-rituals-of-haven-protection-and-clairvoyance-and-similar-powers?p=1557680#post1557680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Completely remote powers (Scrying, Clairvoyance) are countered with powers or Rituals that affect the mind. More often than not a player complaint is that Clairvoyance is overpowered because it can not be detected - but it can, that's what the Awareness ability is for. I would also allow Auspex 1 to highten that sixth sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my chronicles I say Auspex 2 (Aura Perception) will detect such scrying. It isn't necessarily automatic as people can overlook it, but it's there to be viewed.<br /> <br /> My reasoning - which I understand not everyone will accept - is that all such remote viewing creates a kind of sensorium on the Astral Plane (because the person is projecting their mental senses) that &quot;peeks&quot; into the physical world, and that Auspex 2 is sufficient to sense it, just like it can auras. It's part of a rather long document on the Astral Plane I've created for the World of Darkness based on various bits found in the World of Darkness sourcebooks on the Astral as well as my own research into real world occultism.<br /> <br /> I would also allow people who - in Werewolf terms - are on the Periphery detect they are being watched. As well as people who have strong intuition or other psychic awareness, even if they may not technically possess the Awareness ability (as it's a non-standard Ability that may get overlooked by the ST).<br /> <br /> Another possible option is to allow some animals to detect such things. Animals definitely detect ghosts, and I'd think it'd be reasonable if they could also other kinds of non-physical intruders. Dogs are known to bark at &quot;something&quot; in an empty room. Why not them as well?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557676-rituals-of-haven-protection-and-clairvoyance-and-similar-powers?p=1557680#post1557680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think some kinks in the protection of a Haven <i>should </i>be difficult to cover, at the very least for the benefit of players of Clans or splats that are able to exploit them - if I make warding Havens against Wraith spies too easy, I take that option away from the Giovanni player.</div> </div> </div> </div>These situations can be hard for the ST to adjudicate. You need to allow those characters (especially PCs) get good mileage out of their powers and abilities. At the same time, supernatural creatures with sufficient experience are going to realize this is a big security problem and will take steps against it, and I dislike the idea that the <i>only</i> options that exist must be highly trained magicians like Tremere, Giovanni, Sorcerers, or Mages.<br /> <br /> In Wraith, it's explicitly said ordinary people can ward and banish ghosts using just their Willpower provided they engage in folkloric activities they truly believe are effective. So I'm open to these kind of things. However, it's a fine line. You don't want <i>nothing</i> to be able to detect (or even stop) such supernatural spying or intruders, but you still want some NPCs to be able to block it. Options have to be available to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-17T17:06:54-08:00","id":1557718,"title":"","content":"There's a big if here.<br /> <br /> If the Cainite enter the haven before and got burned, it knows it limit range approximately. Then on if the Cainite want to enter via Astral Projection it most probably can't do it since it's still a vampire's soul trying to do so. Of course depending on the knowledge of both parties I'd might rule to have contested Willpower rolls.<br /> <br /> Wardings can be:<br /> - Ward versus Kindred level 4<br /> - Warding Circle versus Kindred level 4<br /> - Dedicate Chantry level 1<br /> - Deny the Intruder level 2<br /> - Consecration of Sanctum level 4<br /> - Eyes of Ever Vigland level 7<br /> <br /> and all their alterations:<br /> - Vires Acquirit Eundo level 5<br /> - Lesser Triger level 5<br /> - Greater Trigger level 6<br /> - Suspension of Incancation level 4<br /> <br /> It mostly depends on who against who.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T18:33:39-07:00","id":1562326,"title":"","content":"IME the best way to deal with this without too much rules is to make warding sensory powers more granular.<br /> <br /> The Astral is too close to the Material (if using Mage rules for cosmology, it's probably in the Astral Vidare of the Penumbra). Here it surely works, though may be weaker.<br /> <br /> Against actual sensory powers a normal Ward won't do, although most users will know that and take it into account.<br /> <br /> Wards against Sensory or other interventions work for very specific effects. One can ward against Clairvoyance, another against sensory hijacking, most only work if the effect comes from a certain splat.<br /> <br /> Such wards don't have to be hard to do. Would not cost XP to learn, probably wouldn't require much Blood, or none at all. They can be addons of sorts for regular wards. They may be costly to setup or hard to find, but not terribly so. The idea isn't to make &quot;warding against everything&quot; prohibitively costly, but to make such warding an involved process, that requires you to know what you're warding against and deliberately prepare for it.<br /> <br /> Ever tightening your defenses, never completely invulnerable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}